        "original_id": "312ca2c5-d809-5673-a1b9-5a1c37ebf931",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Grand Hyatt New York, Grand Central Terminal, Midtown Manhattan, New York City\n- Hotels: Commodore Hotel\n- People: Donald Trump\n- Events: 1945 NFL Draft\n- Roles: President of the United States\n\nFacts:\n- The Grand Hyatt New York is a hotel located directly east of Grand Central Terminal in Midtown Manhattan, New York City.\n- The hotel originally opened on January 28, 1919, as the Commodore Hotel.\n- The 1945 NFL Draft was held on April 8, 1945, at the Commodore Hotel in New York City, New York.\n- In 1980, Donald Trump modernized the exterior and renovated the interior of the building as his first construction project in Manhattan.\n- Donald Trump, born on June 14, 1946, became the 45th President of the United States on January 20, 2017.",
